  "limitations": [
    "TRANSDUCTIVE RESEARCH MODE: these predictions need a BATCH of unlabeled target spectra from the same unseen adulterant. Metrics from this mode must never be advertised as single-file (inductive) deployment performance.",
    "Each fold uses the WHOLE held-out adulterant (30-90 spectra spanning all ten levels and every brand of that adulterant) as the unlabeled batch; a batch with a different composition (fewer samples, one level, one brand) is a different problem (see the batch-sensitivity run).",
    "Only the target-batch FEATURES are read; target labels are used for scoring only (canary: shuffling them changes nothing). This is still not an inductive protocol: compare with svr_no_adaptation, which uses the same SVR and features without the batch.",
    "Our OT solver is an independent log-domain implementation; ot_svr_pot calls POT the way the authors describe. Their gap quantifies solver sensitivity of the polynomial SVR.",
    "author_pca50/author_pca10 are published-style PCA baselines fitted on source + unlabeled target X with prespecified sizes; the authors' 'PARAFAC-10' column is PCA with 10 components in their code. CORAL/MMD are not reproduced: the authors tune their size on target labels.",
    "Brand imbalance, five folds, one instrument, laboratory binary mixtures: see LOAO-v1 limits.",
    "Published numbers are shown separately and were not measured by ChemiProof; the authors clip predictions to [0, 1], we score unclipped (clipped values are reported as secondary)."
